Section: Tweaks
Homepage: https://github.com/ibrahim2100/albrhi-repo
Description: Pair an Apple Watch running a watchOS your iPhone does not officially support.
 .
 ▍WHAT IT DOES
 iOS refuses to pair with a watch whose watchOS is newer than it expects, and refuses to
 install companion apps onto it. This answers those compatibility questions the way a
 supported pairing would, so setup completes and apps install.
 .
 ▍SWITCHED ON FROM ALBRHI
 Settings › Albrhi › Albrhi Watch. Nothing is patched until the master switch is on —
 this touches pairing, so it is never on because it happened to be installed. A respring
 button sits on the same page, since every change here takes effect at the next launch of
 the process it lives in.
 .
 ▍CREDIT — THE PAIRING CORE IS SOMEONE ELSE'S WORK
 The pairing gate, the capability answers and the NanoRegistry preference writes come
 from watched by 34306 (github.com/34306/watched), used under the MIT licence, whose text
 ships with this package as LICENSE-watched. What this project adds is the master switch,
 the settings page, the diagnostics and the bilingual interface.
 .
 Maintained by Ibrahim Ismail AL-Rahn. Free and open source.
